// oshun/host — the platform layer: NSApp lifecycle, the ObjC-runtime
// bridge, the host-chrome mailbox (a tray ring today; dialogs and
// notifications next), and host.run — the windowless pump that drains
// it where effect arms are callable. Each module owns the ring its
// native sources push into; a pump drains every ring its program's
// arms listen to.
//
// Platform bodies live in gated parts — index.<os>.kz joins only under
// its build flag, so a Windows part file can sit in this directory as
// dormant bytes until its implementation exists. Decls and impls both
// ride the part: the token types (*Tray holding an Id) are
// platform-typed, and the decl surface cannot outlive the bodies that
// honor it.

~[build == macos]part macos
